# SSCRE cache concurrency

- Protect cache check–generate–insert flows from duplicate generation during
  concurrent misses.
- Recheck the cache after waiting for coordination before calling the model.
- Handle duplicate writes from shared or multi-process repositories without
  returning an avoidable server error; under Strategy C, re-run the safety
  validator before returning the raced entry.
- Treat missing cached compatibility metadata as `UNCERTAIN`; never substitute
  current-request metadata for missing entry metadata.
- Synchronize application-scoped metric updates and snapshots.
- Keep structured decision-log schemas consistent across hit, generated, and
  failure paths, using zero values when upstream metrics are unavailable.
- Include a client-visible correlation ID on controlled error responses.
- Validate embedding model and dimension compatibility before semantic reuse.
- When semantic retrieval is disabled, do not call the embedding provider or
  store vector metadata.
- Validate custom embedding results at the API boundary and fail closed without
  caching invalid vectors.
- Add deterministic tests for repeated generation counts and cache isolation;
  add concurrency and failure-observability coverage when changing those
  behaviors, including semantic retrieval changes.
- Keep coordination bounded and document any intentional serialization or
  distributed-coordination limitation.
